    "q-100563": {
      "dom_id": "step-q100563",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "If ${log}_{7}⁡(a-3)=4$, then $a=$",
      "worked_solution": "To remove the logarithm, we exponentiate both sides of the equation. The base of the logarithm is $7,$ so we use this base for the exponentiation as well:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{7}⁡(a-3) & =4 \\\\ {7}^{{log}_{7}⁡(a-3)} & ={7}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since exponentiation is the inverse function of the logarithm, we get ${7}^{{log}_{7}⁡(a-3)}=a-3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a-3 & ={7}^{4} \\\\ a-3 & =2401 \\\\ a & =2404.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-100563-a",
